/*
  SettingsSearch.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0215 · SettingsSearch (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface (table "SettingsSearch"). Every key the native
  `SettingsSearch` resolves lives here with its English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a per-surface table so
  each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without editing the shared catalog.

  The first three keys are the ones extracted from the web source
  (features/settings/components/SettingsSearch.tsx — `settings.search.placeholder`,
  `settings.search.label`, `settings.search.noResults`). The `search.entries.*` keys are the verbatim
  port of features/settings/searchIndex.ts (`getSettingsIndex`) — same keys + English fallbacks the web
  `t(key, default)` uses. The remaining `settingsSearch.*` keys back the native state envelope (field
  role / clear, idle / loading / empty / error chrome, the freshness chip, the connectivity banner) and
  the accessibility summaries — none of which exist as English literals in the Swift sources.
*/

